   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving overheating, smoke, fire, injury, or property damage to the regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, including incidents initially suspected to involve another cause. They must notify affected customers within 24 hours when the incident involves their unit or presents a credible risk to their model, provide immediate safety instructions, and update them as material facts emerge. A detailed incident report must be submitted to the regulator within 10 calendar days, with a final investigation report within 30 days or an explanation and revised date. Manufacturers must maintain incident records and promptly correct incomplete or missed reports."
