   "rule_summary": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before market entry and at least annually thereafter. The maximum allowed failure rate is 5% for any model.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: over_limit_consequence, transition",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before market entry and at least annually thereafter. Manufacturers must submit per-model results, including sample size and failures, confidentially to the regulator and provide the model’s test date, sample size, number of failures, and failure rate to customers buying or owning it. Results must not be published to the general public by company and model. The maximum allowed failure rate is 5% for any model. A model exceeding 5% must be promptly reported to the regulator and undergo a regulator-reviewed corrective-action plan and retesting on a regulator-set schedule. The regulator may require additional measures, including sales restrictions, where results indicate elevated or imminent serious risk."
  },
