   "rule_summary": "A mandatory recall is triggered when any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in a year. The rate must be calculated from documented incidents and installed-unit counts for the same model and period and reported to the regulator.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must promptly notify affected customers and the regulator of a thermal incident involving their unit, provide safe-use and response instructions, and update customers as the investigation develops. A mandatory recall is triggered when any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in a year. The rate must be calculated from documented incidents and installed-unit counts for the same model and period and reported to the regulator. A recall requires prompt customer notice and an effective remedy, which may include repair, replacement, or refund; a recall is not, by itself, a prohibition on future sales. The regulator may also require a recall sooner where the evidence indicates an imminent serious risk. Recall notices must explain the hazard, affected units, and remedy."
  }
